  "helpStartTitle": "Learn to run Mi Cafetal",
  "helpTabStart": "Start",
  "helpTabRoutine": "Routine",
  "helpTabUnderstand": "Understand",
  "helpStartSubtitle": "Choose how your farm is today. In five minutes you'll make your first entry.",
  "helpStartQuestion": "How is your farm today?",
  "helpStartNote": "Examples use round numbers and “your currency.” They work the same for any country and any crop.",
  "helpCaseSellingTitle": "I already sell what I harvest",
  "helpCaseSellingDesc": "You have crops producing fruit and want to know if you're making money.",
  "helpCaseStartingTitle": "I'm about to start",
  "helpCaseStartingDesc": "You're going to plant and want to see how much you invest before harvesting.",
  "helpCaseRenewTitle": "I'm going to renew or expand",
  "helpCaseRenewDesc": "You're going to replace plants or add area to a crop.",
  "helpCaseWorkersTitle": "I have workers",
  "helpCaseWorkersDesc": "You pay daily wages and want the cost to land on the right crop.",
  "helpSellingIntro": "Don't record what already happened. Start today: what you spend and what you sell.",
  "helpSellingStep1": "Check your crops: Crops › your crop. Set the phase to “Producing” and, if you know them, the area and plants. If you don't, leave them empty: the app doesn't invent.",
  "helpSellingStep2": "Record your first expense: Record › Expense. Choose the crop and category: fertilizer, labor, transport. If the expense is for several crops, split it by area or percentage.",
  "helpSellingStep3": "Record your first sale: Record › Income. Enter the kilos and what you were paid. With those kilos, that crop's harvest is recorded automatically. Don't record it twice.",
  "helpSellingStep4": "Check the month: Overview or Report. There you see income, expenses, balance and cost per kilo. The report exports to PDF or Excel.",
  "helpSellingExampleTitle": "Example with coffee, 2 ha and 3,000 plants",
  "helpSellingExample1": "Expense: 500 in fertilizer, assigned to coffee.",
  "helpSellingExample2": "Sale: 50 kg for 750.",
  "helpSellingExample3": "Result: income 750 · expenses 500 · balance 250 · cost per kilo 10.",
  "helpSellingClosing": "What you sold before using the app isn't needed: the report starts with what you record.",
  "helpSellingMulti": "If you have several crops on the same land, assign them when you record the expense; the app splits it by area or percentage.",
  "helpStartingIntro": "While the crop isn't producing, the app doesn't tell you that you're losing money: it shows how much you've invested. It's an investment, not a bad month.",
  "helpStartingStep1": "Create the crop: Crops › New crop. Name, phase “Not producing yet” and whether it's perennial or annual. Area and plants can stay empty.",
  "helpStartingStep2": "Record the planting: Plantings › New planting. How many plants, in what area and the date. If you enter the cost, the app creates the linked expense for you: don't repeat it in Record.",
  "helpStartingStep3": "Record what you invest: Record › Expense, with the crop. Fertilizer, labor, tools. Everything before the first harvest shows as investment.",
  "helpStartingStep4": "When you harvest, change the phase: Crops › your crop › phase “Producing.” From then on, the sale records the harvest.",
  "helpStartingExampleTitle": "Example with corn, 1 ha and 20,000 plants",
  "helpStartingExample1": "Planting: 20,000 plants on 1 ha.",
  "helpStartingExample2": "Investment: 300 in seed + 200 in preparation = 500.",
  "helpStartingExample3": "Before harvesting: 500 invested, no loss.",
  "helpStartingExample4": "First sale: 1,000 kg for 800. The harvest is recorded.",
  "helpRenewIntro": "Don't delete the old crop. The app keeps its history and adds the new part.",
  "helpRenewStep1": "Choose what happens to the old plants: Plantings › New planting. If you replace part of them, choose “Renew a part” and the lot you're renewing. Old plants go down and new ones add up: the total doesn't inflate.",
  "helpRenewStep2": "If you're expanding, don't replace: choose “Expand the crop.” You add area and plants without touching what was already there.",
  "helpRenewStep3": "Check the new age: the renewed lot starts its own age. Old harvests stay in the history and in the report.",
  "helpRenewExampleTitle": "Example with 3,000 coffee plants; you renew 1,000",
  "helpRenewExample1": "Planting: 1,000 new plants, “Renew a part,” old lot.",
  "helpRenewExample2": "Total: still 3,000, not 4,000.",
  "helpRenewExample3": "The new lot has its date; the old one keeps its own.",
  "helpWorkersCaseIntro": "A wage isn't a loose expense: it goes to the crop where they worked. That's how cost per kilo tells the truth.",
  "helpWorkersStep1": "Save the worker: Workers › New worker. Name and daily pay. If the wage changes, update it there.",
  "helpWorkersStep2": "Record the payment: Record › Expense › Labor. Choose the worker, the days and the crop. The app calculates the amount; if you paid something else, adjust it.",
  "helpWorkersStep3": "If it was harvest work, mark it: in the task choose “Harvest,” enter the kilos and the lot. That gives you the pickup cost per kilo.",
  "helpWorkersStep4": "Check payroll: Report › Payroll of the period. There you see how many days and how much you paid each person.",
  "helpWorkersExampleTitle": "Example with two workers at 20 per day",
  "helpWorkersExample1": "Juan: 3 days on coffee = 60.",
  "helpWorkersExample2": "Pedro: 2 days on coffee = 40.",
  "helpWorkersExample3": "Payroll: 5 days and 100. If it was harvest work, the kilos go to the lot.",
  "helpExampleNote": "Example numbers, in your currency.",
  "helpRoutineTitle": "The routine that makes the app work",
  "helpRoutineIntro": "You don't need to fill everything in. With these four moments, the report builds itself.",
  "helpRoutineWhen": "When",
  "helpRoutineWhat": "What you record",
  "helpRoutineWhere": "Where",
  "helpRoutineRow1When": "Every expense",
