  "glossaryTitle": "What do these terms mean?",
  "glossaryGotIt": "Got it",
  "glossaryIncomeTerm": "Income",
  "glossaryIncomeDef": "What you were paid for what you sold. It's not the same as harvesting: you can harvest and not sell.",
  "glossaryExpenseTerm": "Expense",
  "glossaryExpenseDef": "What you paid to produce or maintain the farm. If it belongs to a crop, assign it.",
  "glossaryRoiTerm": "ROI (Return on Investment)",
  "glossaryRoiDef": "Measures how much you recover for every 100 invested in a crop. It is calculated as (Income - Expenses) ÷ Expenses. A negative ROI means the crop spends more than it recovers: for example, an ROI of -70% means that for every 100 invested only 30 come back.",
  "glossaryBalanceTerm": "Balance / Result",
  "glossaryBalanceDef": "Income minus Expenses in a period. If the result is positive you have a gain; if negative, a loss.",
  "glossaryMarginTerm": "Margin on sales",
  "glossaryMarginDef": "Of every 100 you sell, how much remains as profit after covering expenses. A margin of 20% means that for every 100 sold, 20 remain.",
  "glossaryRatioTerm": "Expenses vs income",
  "glossaryRatioDef": "What percentage of your income goes to expenses. For example, 80% means that for every 100 that come in, 80 are spent and 20 remain.",
  "glossaryAvgTerm": "Monthly historical average",
  "glossaryAvgDef": "The average of what you spend per month in a category (for example, labor). It serves as a reference to detect unusual increases in your expenses.",
  "glossaryYieldAreaTerm": "Yield per area (kg/ha)",
  "glossaryYieldAreaDef": "How many kilos you get from one hectare. It lets you compare lots of different sizes: if one gives 1,200 kg/ha and another 800 kg/ha, the first yields more from the same land.",
  "glossaryYieldPlantTerm": "Yield per plant (kg/plant)",
  "glossaryYieldPlantDef": "How many kilos each plant produces. It helps you tell whether the problem is the number of plants or how the crop is being cared for.",
  "glossaryCostPerKgTerm": "Total cost per kg",
  "glossaryCostPerKgDef": "Everything it cost you to produce each kilo (establishment, labor and the period's expenses) divided by the kilos harvested. If you sell below this number, you lose money.",
  "glossaryPickupCostTerm": "Picking cost per kg",
  "glossaryPickupCostDef": "What you pay to pick one kilo: day labor and collection, not counting what you invested in planting. It is the immediate cost of each harvest.",
  "glossaryEstablishmentTerm": "Establishment investment",
  "glossaryEstablishmentDef": "What you invested to start the crop: seedlings, initial fertilizer and the labor of planting. It is not a loss, it is an investment you recover through sales.",
  "glossaryPaybackTerm": "Payback (recovery)",
  "glossaryPaybackDef": "How long it takes you to recover what you invested in establishment. 100% means you have already paid it off completely with what you sold.",
  "glossarySubtotalTerm": "Subtotal",
  "glossarySubtotalDef": "A partial sum of a group of rows before the grand total. In payroll it is what each worker is paid before the period total.",
  "glossaryYtdTerm": "Year to date (YTD)",
  "glossaryYtdDef": "What has accumulated from January 1 of this year until today, no matter which month you are looking at.",
  "glossaryPayrollTerm": "Payroll for the period",
  "glossaryPayrollDef": "What was paid for labor in the period: people, days worked and day labor. It does not include what you invest in planting.",
  "glossaryCashBoxTerm": "Petty cash",
  "glossaryCashBoxDef": "Money available for small monthly expenses: transport, tools and emergencies. It is compared against the budget you set so you do not overspend.",
  "glossarySoldVsHarvestedTerm": "Sold vs harvested",
  "glossarySoldVsHarvestedDef": "Compares the kilos you sold with the kilos you harvested in the same period. If you sold more, it is usually a harvest from earlier months or one you have not recorded.",
  "glossaryRoiTooltip": "What does ROI mean?",

